on": "T Mục A: “His days stretched to a little over twenty-four hours” — trong hang không đồng hồ, không ánh sáng, không radio. Bẫy: thí sinh dễ nhớ chi tiết “tưởng ngày tháng sớm hơn một tháng” mà quên rằng câu hỏi chỉ hỏi về độ dài chu kỳ sinh học."}, {"n": 74, "text": "Aschoff’s volunteers lost their rhythm altogether once every external time cue had been removed.", "typ": "choice", "options": {"T": "T", "F": "F", "NG": "NG"}, "answer": "F", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "F Mục A: “stripped of every external cue, human beings do not become arrhythmic. They keep time, but slightly badly.” Trực tiếp phủ định “lost their rhythm altogether”."}, {"n": 75, "text": "The period gene was the first circadian gene ever identified in any living organism.", "typ": "choice", "options": {"T": "T", "F": "F", "NG": "NG"}, "answer": "NG", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "NG Mục B chỉ kể việc nhân dòng gene period và giải Nobel 2017; không có câu nào khẳng định đây là gene nhịp sinh học đầu tiên được tìm ra ở bất kỳ sinh vật nào. Bẫy suy diễn từ “isolated a gene they named period”."}, {"n": 76, "text": "Peripheral clocks stop oscillating as soon as their connection with the brain is broken.", "typ": "choice", "options": {"T": "T", "F": "F", "NG": "NG"}, "answer": "F", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "F Mục B: “these peripheral clocks go on oscillating for days after all connection with the brain has been severed.”"}, {"n": 77, "text": "Blind people whose melanopsin cells survive sleep better than sighted people who work nights.", "typ": "choice", "options": {"T": "T", "F": "F", "NG": "NG"}, "answer": "NG", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "NG Mục B chỉ nói người mù (do hỏng tế bào que–nón) vẫn có thể được đồng bộ nếu tế bào melanopsin còn sống; không hề so sánh chất lượng giấc ngủ của họ với người làm ca đêm."}, {"n": 78, "text": "Later school start times have produced clear and undisputed gains in academic performance.", "typ": "choice", "options": {"T": "T", "F": "F", "NG": "NG"}, "answer": "F", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "F Mục C: “the effect on grades has been more modest, and remains contested.” Trái với “clear and undisputed gains”."}, {"n": 79, "text": "The 2007 classification of shift work rested on stronger evidence from animals than from humans.", "typ": "choice", "options": {"T": "T", "F": "F", "NG": "NG"}, "answer": "T", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "T Mục D: “limited evidence in humans and sufficient evidence in animals” — bằng chứng ở động vật mạnh hơn ở người."}, {"n": 80, "text": "Which section mentions an organism that maintained its rhythm after being deprived of light?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "A", "B": "B", "C": "C", "D": "D"}, "answer": "A", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "A “he shut the plant inside a cupboard where no daylight could reach it and found that the leaves went on opening and closing” — cây mimosa."}, {"n": 81, "text": "Which section describes a self-cancelling cycle in which a substance shuts down its own production?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "A", "B": "B", "C": "C", "D": "D"}, "answer": "B", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "B “that protein blocks the very gene that produces it, so its own levels fall… a self-cancelling feedback loop”."}, {"n": 82, "text": "Which section reports a laboratory result concerning the timing of food rather than its quantity?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "A", "B": "B", "C": "C", "D": "D"}, "answer": "D", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "D “mice given the same number of calories during their rest phase rather than their active phase put on more weight” — cùng lượng calo, khác thời điểm."}, {"n": 83, "text": "Which section gives a figure for the average mismatch between biological and imposed sleep timing?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "A", "B": "B", "C": "C", "D": "D"}, "answer": "C", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "C “In industrialised populations the average gap exceeds an hour” — độ lệch giữa giờ sinh học và giờ thời khóa biểu."}, {"n": 84, "text": "Which section notes that light signals used for timekeeping bypass the region of the brain used for seeing?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "A", "B": "B", "C": "C", "D": "D"}, "answer": "B", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "B “send their signal not to the visual cortex but straight to the suprachiasmatic nucleus”."}, {"n": 85, "text": "Which section refers to an investigator who lost track of the calendar?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "A", "B": "B", "C": "C", "D": "D"}, "answer": "A", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "A “he believed the date to be a month earlier than it was” — Michel Siffre."}, {"n": 86, "text": "Which section cites evidence that a widely assumed sleep norm may be set too high?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "A", "B": "B", "C": "C", "D": "D"}, "answer": "D", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "D “the industrialised eight-hour ideal may be a poor benchmark” + số liệu 5,5–7 giờ ở ba xã hội tiền công nghiệp."}, {"n": 87, "text": "Which section explains how a person’s preferred sleep timing changes across the lifespan?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "A", "B": "B", "C": "C", "D": "D"}, "answer": "C", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 3", "explanation": "C “Children are early risers; the clock delays sharply at puberty, reaches its latest point at around twenty, and then advances steadily.”"}, {"n": 88, "text": "What is the writer’s main aim in paragraph 1?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "To explain why the earliest collections were assembled without any organising principle.", "B": "To show that early collectors valued natural specimens more highly than man-made ones.", "C": "To argue that the apparent disorder of the cabinet followed a logic modern viewers no longer share.", "D": "To trace the origins of modern scientific taxonomy to seventeenth-century private collectors."}, "answer": "C", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 4", "explanation": "C Đoạn 1: “To modern eyes the arrangement looks like chaos. It was not. The cabinet obeyed a principle that has since fallen out of use.” Mục đích của đoạn là bác bỏ ấn tượng “hỗn loạn”. Loại A (trái nghĩa trực tiếp); loại D vì bài nói rõ Ole Worm xếp theo chain of being rather than a taxonomy; loại B vì bài nhấn mạnh sự đặt cạnh nhau của tự nhiên và nhân tạo, không xếp hạng cao thấp."}, {"n": 89, "text": "What does the account of the Ashmolean’s foundation suggest?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "Ashmole’s title to the collection he handed over was not universally accepted.", "B": "Oxford was reluctant to take the collection on the terms it was offered.", "C": "Tradescant had always intended his collection to end up in a university.", "D": "The building was finished before the collection was moved into it."}, "answer": "A", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 4", "explanation": "A Đoạn 2: “a collection he had acquired — not without controversy — from the family of the gardener and traveller John Tradescant”. Cụm chêm phủ định kép hàm ý quyền sở hữu của Ashmole từng bị tranh cãi. Loại B (Oxford chấp nhận điều kiện, xây nhà và mở cửa 1683); loại C (bài không nói gì về ý định của Tradescant); loại D (điều kiện là “a building be put up to house it”, tức nhà xây sau khi hiến)."}, {"n": 90, "text": "Why is Cole’s competition with the public house mentioned?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "To explain why gas lighting had to be installed in the galleries.", "B": "To suggest that evening opening proved unpopular with museum staff.", "C": "To indicate that museums of the period were chronically short of money.", "D": "To make clear that the museum’s improving mission was aimed at a particular class."}, "answer": "D", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 4", "explanation": "D Đoạn 3: Cole mở cửa buổi tối, thắp đèn ga “so that working people might come after their shifts” rồi “competing with the public house” — đích nhắm là tầng lớp lao động. A và C đảo ngược quan hệ nhân quả; B không có trong bài."}, {"n": 91, "text": "The writer’s presentation of the 2002 Declaration implies that", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "its signatories succeeded in bringing the restitution debate to an end.", "B": "the authority of the document was weakened by the narrowness of its membership.", "C": "it was drafted in direct response to the return of material taken from Benin City.", "D": "the majority of its signatories have since publicly reversed their position."}, "answer": "B", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 4", "explanation": "B Đoạn 4: “Critics observed that no museum outside Europe and North America had been invited to sign.” Câu này chỉ có tác dụng làm suy yếu tính đại diện — tức là thẩm quyền — của Tuyên bố. Loại A (tranh luận vẫn tiếp diễn, “since 2018 the argument has moved”); loại C (sai trình tự thời gian: 2002 trước 2018); loại D (bài không nói ai đảo ngược lập trường)."}, {"n": 92, "text": "What is the significance of the timing-and-tracking studies described in paragraph 5?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "They exposed a gap between the way museums describe visits and the way visits proceed.", "B": "They demonstrated that visitors prefer temporary exhibitions to permanent collections.", "C": "They proved that museum fatigue can be eliminated by better placement of cases.", "D": "They persuaded museums to reduce the number of objects placed on display."}, "answer": "A", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 4", "explanation": "A Đoạn 5: “The findings have shaped practice rather more than they have shaped rhetoric.” Hàm ý: cách bảo tàng nói về chuyến tham quan khác với cách chuyến tham quan diễn ra. Loại B (không có so sánh sở thích); loại C (Gilman đặt tên cho hiện tượng, không chứng minh cách chữa); loại D (bài nói bảng chú giải ngắn lại và thêm ghế, không nói giảm số hiện vật)."}, {"n": 93, "text": "Where in the passage does the following sentence best fit?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "(I)", "B": "(II)", "C": "(III)", "D": "(IV)"}, "answer": "B", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 4", "explanation": "B — [II] Câu chèn có “Such transfers of ownership” nên phải đứng ngay sau một chuyển giao sở hữu (Sloane → quốc gia, 1759) và ngay trước lời phản chứng cụ thể “In practice admission required a written application”. Ở [I] không có “transfer of ownership” nào; ở [III] mạch đang nói về mở rộng tiếp cận nên “did little to make accessible” là mâu thuẫn; ở [IV] chủ đề đã chuyển sang hành vi người xem."}, {"n": 94, "text": "What is the most likely outcome implied by the final paragraph?", "typ": "choice", "options": {"A": "Museums will progressively abandon free admission to their permanent collections.", "B": "Online provision will in time replace the physical visit for most audiences.", "C": "Blockbuster exhibitions will before long cease to be financially viable.", "D": "The conflict between contemplation and attendance will continue unresolved."}, "answer": "D", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 4", "explanation": "D Đoạn 6: “holding two incompatible ideas at once… Governments, meanwhile, have begun to attach conditions to their subsidies — on free access, on outreach, on the breadth of the audience reached — which pull the institution in a third direction again. Nothing in its history suggests that the tension will be resolved.” Loại A (bài nói bộ sưu tập thường trực vẫn miễn phí ở nhiều nước, không dự báo bỏ); loại B (bài nói trực tuyến bổ sung chứ không thay thế); loại C (blockbuster đang là “financial engine”)."}, {"n": 95, "text": "The earliest forerunners of the museum were private rooms whose contents were arranged to provoke (95)__________, an emotion then regarded as the starting point of knowledge rather than as its opposite. Entry depended on an invitation that advertised the owner’s standing. The shift to public ownership came first through bequest and purchase — the Ashmolean, and then the British Museum, whose acquisition obliged Parliament to compensate Sloane’s (96)__________ — and decisively through revolution, when the royal holdings in the Louvre passed to the nation. Over the following century objects were redistributed into (97)__________ that could themselves be read as arguments, and institutions such as the Victoria and Albert Museum opened at night in order to draw working people away from the (98)__________. The methods of acquisition used in that same century now dominate debate, and since 2018 discussion of restitution has moved from whether to the (99)__________ on which it should proceed. Meanwhile tracking studies have shown that visitors examine few objects and do so briefly, and the temporary blockbuster has become the (100)__________ of many collections.\n\nComplete gap (95) with NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage.", "typ": "text", "options": null, "answer": "wonder", "section": "Reading Comprehension", "part": "Part 4", "explanation": "wonder Đoạn 1: “was meant to provoke wonder, and wonder was understood as the beginning of knowledge rather than as its opposite.” Khung “arranged to provoke ___” chỉ nhận danh từ không đếm được này."}, {"n": 96, "text": "The earliest forerunners of the museum were private rooms whose contents were arranged to provoke (95)__________, an emotion then regarded as the starting point of knowledge rather than as its opposite. Entry depended on an invitation that advertised the owner’s standing. The shift to public ownership came first through bequest and purc